      "id": "lem-each-round-has-polynomial-communication",
      "concern": "Statement clause 3 says each received polynomial is evaluated at 0, 1, and two current points. In def-shamir-protocol-for-tqbf the verifier evaluates s at 0, 1, and the new challenge r_t; a reduction check uses the stored scalar a=σ(i) as a coefficient in (1−a)s(0)+a s(1), not as an evaluation point. Thus the stated evaluation-point/count assertion is false, although the O(D) bound survives with three evaluations.",
      "severity": "would-be-fatal"
    },
