      "id": "lem-lazy-walk-lengths-within-root-t-have-close-endpoint-laws",
      "concern": "Claim 2 compares X_{v,ℓ} and X_{v,ℓ′}, but the setup assumes only R≥ℓ. The definition of X from endpoint-view claims requires each walk length to be at most R, so X_{v,ℓ′} is not defined for all allowed parameters unless R≥max(ℓ,ℓ′). The current powering application uses lengths within R; state the missing radius condition.",
